pe of energy?\nHot water", "options": ["Kinetic", "Chemical", "Gravitational potential", "Thermal"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 3, "model": "Kinetic; chemical; gravitational potential; thermal.", "points": null}, {"id": "b2cea45a-0374-5cb8-8e6c-d8016e5f9b7f", "quiz": "cf6d16f0-3bb9-540b-8954-be5e9214289d", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nDescribe the energy changes when a person eats breakfast and then runs.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "Chemical energy in the food [1] is changed into kinetic energy (and thermal energy) in the muscles [1].", "points": [{"text": "Chemical energy in the food", "any": ["chemical", "food"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Is changed into kinetic energy (and thermal energy) in the muscles", "any": ["kinetic", "thermal", "heat", "movement"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "898e288e-fffa-522b-a621-7a080ae1f7d4", "quiz": "cf6d16f0-3bb9-540b-8954-be5e9214289d", "pos": 7, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion D: Reflecting on the impacts of science]\nMany rural families cook with firewood. Suggest one problem this causes and one cleaner energy source that could replace it.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion D", "correct": null, "model": "Firewood smoke damages the lungs and cutting trees causes deforestation [1]; biogas or LPG gas (or solar cookers) are cleaner [1].", "points": [{"text": "Firewood smoke damages the lungs and cutting trees causes deforestation", "any": ["smoke", "deforest", "trees", "lungs", "pollution", "cough"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Biogas or LPG gas (or solar cookers) are cleaner", "any": ["biogas", "solar", "lpg", "gas", "electric", "clean cookstove"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "e422cc86-455b-56db-9f68-7713617e4d09", "quiz": "e741023c-d5d5-525b-abc9-cc6a619d59f6", "pos": 1, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nState the law of conservation of energy.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "Energy cannot be created or destroyed [1]; it can only be transferred from one form to another [1].", "points": [{"text": "Energy cannot be created or destroyed", "any": ["cannot be created", "not created", "cannot be destroyed", "not destroyed"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "It can only be transferred from one form to another", "any": ["transferred", "changed", "converted", "total"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "84417c3b-b5c4-51f6-afa7-ed942df00e00", "quiz": "e741023c-d5d5-525b-abc9-cc6a619d59f6", "pos": 2, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nCalculate the GPE of a 5 kg box on a shelf 2 m high (g = 10 N/kg).", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "GPE = 5 × 10 × 2 [1] = 100 J [1].", "points": [{"text": "GPE = 5 × 10 × 2", "any": ["5 × 10 × 2", "5 x 10 x 2"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 100 J", "any": ["100"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "845428c5-4a8f-58fb-ab39-a2dafe166f7e", "quiz": "e741023c-d5d5-525b-abc9-cc6a619d59f6", "pos": 3, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nCalculate the KE of a 1000 kg car moving at 10 m/s.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "KE = ½ × 1000 × 10² [1] = 50 000 J [1].", "points": [{"text": "KE = ½ × 1000 × 10²", "any": ["0.5 × 1000 × 100", "½ × 1000 × 10²", "500 × 100", "0.5 x 1000 x 100"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 50 000 J", "any": ["50 000", "50000", "50,000"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "64fbfe70-4609-5d1c-bd49-3004fa6a1477", "quiz": "e741023c-d5d5-525b-abc9-cc6a619d59f6", "pos": 4, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nA 0.2 kg ball is dropped from 5 m. Ignoring air resistance, calculate its kinetic energy just before it hits the ground.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "GPE lost = 0.2 × 10 × 5 [1] = 10 J = KE gained [1].", "points": [{"text": "GPE lost = 0.2 × 10 × 5", "any": ["0.2 × 10 × 5", "0.2 x 10 x 5", "gpe"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 10 J = KE gained", "any": ["10"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "35e31590-b4c1-55bf-9135-4bee0ca974eb", "quiz": "86bb94a7-b76d-5e96-b976-ccf374c3e0c2", "pos": 1, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nState Newton's first law of motion.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "An object stays at rest or moves at a constant speed in a straight line [1] unless a resultant (unbalanced) force acts on it [1].", "points": [{"text": "An object stays at rest or moves at a constant speed in a straight line", "any": ["rest", "stay still", "stationary", "constant speed", "keep moving"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Unless a resultant (unbalanced) force acts on it", "any": ["unless", "resultant force", "unbalanced force", "force acts"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "f3ec0406-f0c3-5fc5-808b-b3981c8a7c8e", "quiz": "86bb94a7-b76d-5e96-b976-ccf374c3e0c2", "pos": 2, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nState Newton's third law of motion.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "When one object pushes on another, the second pushes back with an equal force [1] in the opposite direction [1].", "points": [{"text": "When one object pushes on another, the second pushes back with an equal force", "any": ["equal"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "In the opposite direction", "any": ["opposite"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "dacf337f-77fb-5f55-9887-04824953046e", "quiz": "86bb94a7-b76d-5e96-b976-ccf374c3e0c2", "pos": 3, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nA 40 kg trolley accelerates at 1.5 m/s². Calculate the resultant force.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "F = 40 × 1.5 [1] = 60 N [1].", "points": [{"text": "F = 40 × 1.5", "any": ["40 × 1.5", "40 x 1.5", "40*1.5"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 60 N", "any": ["60"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "d194684a-661b-5ec3-8add-bc6762678c15", "quiz": "86bb94a7-b76d-5e96-b976-ccf374c3e0c2", "pos": 4, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nExplain why it is harder to stop a loaded lorry than an empty one moving at the same speed.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "The loaded lorry has more mass and so more inertia [1], so a bigger force (or a longer time and distance) is needed to stop it [1].", "points": [{"text": "The loaded lorry has more mass and so more inertia", "any": ["more mass", "heavier", "greater mass", "inertia"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A bigger force (or a longer time and distance) is needed to stop it", "any": ["more force", "bigger force", "longer", "f = m", "more distance"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "e62d0ca3-e641-55e8-a766-7d09cf6de26c", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 1, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich simple machine?\nA ramp into a lorry", "options": ["Lever", "Pulley", "Inclined plane"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 2, "model": "Ramp: inclined plane; bottle opener: lever; well wheel: pulley.", "points": null}, {"id": "bc0a0084-fb95-52e7-8762-e133af056c22", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 2, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich simple machine?\nA bottle opener", "options": ["Lever", "Pulley", "Inclined plane"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 0, "model": "Ramp: inclined plane; bottle opener: lever; well wheel: pulley.", "points": null}, {"id": "269c6721-167f-51fd-a036-60657e378760", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 3, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich simple machine?\nA bucket raised from a well by a rope over a wheel", "options": ["Lever", "Pulley", "Inclined plane"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 1, "model": "Ramp: inclined plane; bottle opener: lever; well wheel: pulley.", "points": null}, {"id": "7b43419b-a6f4-51ae-8d1a-b6fc43d7f435", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 4, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nCalculate the moment of a 20 N force acting 0.5 m from a pivot.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "Moment = 20 × 0.5 [1] = 10 N m [1].", "points": [{"text": "Moment = 20 × 0.5", "any": ["20 × 0.5", "20 x 0.5"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 10 N m", "any": ["10"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "a4d306b7-0357-5790-9589-a205d518a0ff", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 5, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nAn electric motor uses 500 J and gives 450 J of useful kinetic energy. Calculate its efficiency.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "450 ÷ 500 [1] × 100 = 90% [1].", "points": [{"text": "450 ÷ 500", "any": ["450 ÷ 500", "450/500", "0.9"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "× 100 = 90%", "any": ["90"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "3d2d1ad1-dab2-5f11-8134-65fc7c7a8b77", "quiz": "5c7c6431-5c2f-5d0f-8341-0dc7e7735c81", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion D: Reflecting on the impacts of science]\nSuggest two ways schools in Kenya could reduce carbon dioxide emissions from machines and transport.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion D", "correct": null, "model": "Use solar panels and electric school buses instead of diesel generators and buses [1]; encourage walking or cycling to school and switch off machines when not in use (or plant trees) [1].", "points": [{"text": "Use solar panels and electric school buses instead of diesel generators and buses", "any": ["solar", "renewable", "electric", "walk", "cycle", "bus"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Encourage walking or cycling to school and switch off machines when not in use (or plant trees)", "any": ["trees", "switch off", "efficient", "cookstove", "biogas", "carpool", "maintenance"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}], "subject": "MYP Physics", "level": "Grade 6", "unit": "MYP 1 · Physics · Motion, forces and energy", "first": 29, "cfirst": 28, "k": 9}$j$::jsonb; t uuid := (d->'topic'->>'id')::uuid; begin
  if (d->'topic'->>'new')::boolean then
    insert into public.topics (id, subject_id, programme, name, summary, sort_order, parent_id) select t, s.id, d->'topic'->>'programme', d->'topic'->>'name', d->'topic'->>'summary', (d->'topic'->>'sort')::int, (d->'topic'->>'parent')::uuid
      from public.subjects s where s.name = 'MYP Science' on conflict (id) do nothing;
  end if;
  insert into public.lessons (id, topic_id, title, summary, url, external_id, max_marks, sort_order) select (l->>'id')::uuid, t, l->>'title', l->>'summary', l->>'url', l->>'ext', (l->>'max')::int, (l->>'sort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (external_id) do update set title = excluded.title, url = excluded.url, max_marks = excluded.max_marks, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;
  insert into public.lesson_specs (lesson, title, spec, updated_at) select l->>'ext', l->>'title', l->'spec', now() from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (lesson) do update set title = excluded.title, spec = excluded.spec, updated_at = now();
  if not exists (select 1 from public.materials m join jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l on m.path = l->>'url') then   -- make room once: everything after the anchor moves down
    update public.materials set sort = sort + (d->>'k')::int where sort >= (d->>'first')::int;
    update public.class_materials cm set sort = cm.sort + (d->>'k')::int where cm.sort >= (d->>'cfirst')::int and cm.class_id in (select a.class_id from public.class_materials a where a.path = d->>'anchor');
  end if;
  insert into public.materials (path, lesson_id, title, kind, subject, level, unit, sort) select l->>'url', l->>'ext', l->>'title', 'lesson', d->>'subject', d->>'level', d->>'unit', (l->>'msort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (path) do update set lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, subject = excluded.subject, level = excluded.level, unit = excluded.unit, sort = excluded.sort;
  insert into public.class_materials (class_id, path, sort) select a.class_id, l->>'url', (l->>'csort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l join public.class_materials a on a.path = d->>'anchor' on conflict do nothing;
  insert into public.quizzes (id, topic_id, title, instructions, time_limit_minutes, max_attempts, published, show_results, category, feedback_mode, created_by)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, t, q->>'title', q->>'instr', null, 2, true, true, 'quiz', 'hybrid', 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q
    on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, instructions = excluded.instructions, topic_id = excluded.topic_id;
  if exists (select 1 from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'quizzes' and column_name = 'subject') then
    update public.quizzes set subject = 'Physics' where id in (select (q->>'id')::uuid from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q);
  end if;
  insert into public.questions (id, topic_id, kind, prompt, options, marks, section, created_by) select (q->>'id')::uuid, t, q->>'kind', q->>'prompt', q->'options', (q->>'marks')::int, q->>'section', 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (id) do update set prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, marks = excluded.marks, kind = excluded.kind, section = excluded.section;
  insert into public.question_answers (question_id, correct_option, model_answer, mark_scheme, points, explanation)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, (q->>'correct')::int, case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then q->'options'->>((q->>'correct')::int) else q->>'model' end, case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then null else q->>'model' end,
           case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then null else q->'points' end, q->>'model' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (question_id) do update set correct_option = excluded.correct_option, model_answer = excluded.model_answer, mark_scheme = excluded.mark_scheme, points = excluded.points, explanation = excluded.explanation;
  insert into public.quiz_questions (quiz_id, question_id, position) select (q->>'quiz')::uuid, (q->>'id')::uuid, (q->>'pos')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (quiz_id, question_id) do update set position = excluded.position;
  insert into public.quiz_classes (quiz_id, class_id, published, published_at, published_by)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, c.id, c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e', case when c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' then now() end, case when c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' then 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e'::uuid end
      from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q cross join public.classes c where c.id in (select a.class_id from public.class_materials a where a.path = d->>'anchor')
    on conflict do nothing;
end $do$;
select (select count(*) from public.lessons where external_id like 'G6-PHYS-MOTION-L%') as lessons, (select count(*) from public.lesson_specs where lesson like 'G6-PHYS-MOTION-L%') as specs, (select count(*) from public.materials where path like '/g6-phys-motion-%') as materials, (select count(*) from public.class_materials where path like '/g6-phys-motion-%') as class_links, (select count(*) from public.quizzes where topic_id = '254abfba-0be1-55fd-a799-860171719b52' and title like '%exam-style questions') as exam_sets, (select count(*) from public.quiz_questions qq join public.quizzes q on q.id = qq.quiz_id where q.topic_id = '254abfba-0be1-55fd-a799-860171719b52' and q.title like '%exam-style questions') as exam_questions;
